DATA SOURCES
------------
- Real-time hot lists are fetched from each platform's own public,
  unofficial-but-open web interfaces. All content, trademarks and data remain
  the property of their respective platforms; TrendHub only normalizes and
  presents them, and every record carries its sourceUrl.
- Google Trends interest-over-time and related-queries are read from Google's
  public explore widgets. Values are RELATIVE popularity on a 0-100 scale, not
  absolute search volumes. Google's legacy Daily/Realtime Trending endpoints
  (JSON and RSS) were retired by Google and are intentionally not used.
- Future-signal headlines come from each publication's public RSS feed;
  headlines/abstracts are © their publishers and are used for trend research.
- Xiaohongshu (小红书 / RED): the default zero-login path activates an anonymous
  guest web session and reads the public home-feed of trending notes (titles,
  authors, covers, and platform-displayed like counts such as "4.1万"/"10万+",
  which are approximate display strings, not exact integers). The official
  search hot-word board and keyword search require a real logged-in cookie
  (XHS_COOKIE); without it those views are explicitly marked unavailable and no
  data is fabricated. Content is © Xiaohongshu and its respective authors.

